.TH ELDRINTH 6 "November 2026" "ELDRINTH 1.4" "Games"
.SH NAME
eldrinth \- The Unbound Spire, an offline dark fantasy action RPG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eldrinth
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explore four frontier regions, enter nine shard fortresses, investigate records,
and choose the fate of the conscious people held by the Unbound Spire.
The game includes its desktop runtime and plays without network access.
.SH CONTROLS
Move with WASD or arrow keys. Attack with J or Space, dash with Shift,
parry with F, interact with E, raise the lantern with R, and switch tools with Q.
Open equipment with I, the journal with L, and the atlas with M.
Escape or P pauses the game. F11 toggles fullscreen.
Primary keyboard bindings can be changed under Pause, Controls.
Standard gamepads support movement and combat; see the Controls panel for mappings.
.SH SAVES
Three save slots are available. Progress autosaves during play and on normal exit.
The title screen can export a slot as a JSON backup and restore a backup into an
empty slot. Browser and desktop saves can be transferred with these backups.
Package upgrades and removal preserve user saves.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/eldrinth
Desktop saves and preferences. Defaults to ~/.config/eldrinth.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/eldrinth
Release notes, license notices and packaging documentation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ELDRINTH_USER_DATA_DIR
Override the desktop profile directory. Use an absolute path.
.SH CONTENT
Mature themes include institutional violence and death. A first-launch notice
appears before play.
